From 3c260a82aa5333e13641ecbe0b97af86dd84bc26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: powerlaw contributor <contributor@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:08:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix discrete random generation: exact integer inverse search,
 floor in the discrete estimate

_double_search_discrete bisected a continuous x with tol=0.5 and truncated it,
which is exact only when xmin is a power of two; for other xmin about 15% of
quantiles landed on the wrong integer and the generated P(k) was not even
monotone. It now searches over integers (doubling step, then integer
bisection) for the largest k with ccdf(k) >= 1 - r, clipped at xmax. u = 0
returns xmin (it raised a TypeError), a non-integer xmin raises a clear
ValueError, and a ccdf that never falls raises a RuntimeError instead of
looping forever.

_generate_random_discrete_estimate rounded (xmin - 1/2)(1 - r)^(-1/(alpha-1))
+ 1/2 instead of flooring it (Clauset et al. 2009, Appendix D), halving the
probability of xmin (0.074 instead of 0.139 for alpha = 2.5, xmin = 10). The
xmax bound of the approximate path now aims between the steps xmax - 1 and
xmax, and values are clipped to stay under xmax.

Adds testing/test_discrete_generation.py: deterministic quantile grids
against an independent mpmath Hurwitz-zeta oracle.
---
 powerlaw/distributions.py           | 101 +++++++++-----
 testing/test_discrete_generation.py | 205 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 273 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 testing/test_discrete_generation.py

